<%# locals: (page:, head:, status:, chat:, turns: 0) %>
<%#
  ONE structure for every page where a visitor talks to an agent
  (.agents/epics/build-with-ray-v2.md, section 6): /build, /build/:token and
  /applications/:slug/chat. Top to bottom:

    head     the agent's portrait, centered (agent_chats/_header)
    status   the page's status card: the heading on /build; the app's title over
             Agent · Theme · Domain on a draft (build/_status_card); the app's
             Building · Releasing · Deploying and its tokens on the app chat
             (agent_chats/_devops_card)
    chat     the thread, then the chat box (agent_chats/_form)

  Each slot is ready markup. The three pages share it, and each slot keeps a
  view-transition name, so a move between them (Turbo, with
  <meta name="view-transition">) changes only what differs.

  AS THE CONVERSATION GROWS (task build-launch-chat-growth): the shell is a
  column no taller than the window under the navbar. The thread grows with its
  turns until the shell reaches that height; then the thread scrolls inside it,
  the chat box stays at the window's bottom, and whatever sits below the shell
  (/build's gallery, the footer) is pushed off screen. The head and status card
  compact in steps as turns accumulate (data-shell-size: full, medium, compact;
  AgentShellHelper), so the conversation takes about 40% of the window at first
  and about 80% later. `turns` sets the first step on the server, so a reload
  paints at its size; app/javascript/agent_shell.js moves it on as turns arrive,
  never back, and app/assets/tailwind/agent_shell.css draws each step, animated
  unless the visitor prefers reduced motion.
%>
<section class="agent-shell max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-4 sm:pt-8 flex flex-col gap-6" data-test="agent-shell" data-shell="<%= page %>"
         data-agent-shell data-shell-size="<%= agent_shell_size(turns) %>"
         data-shell-medium-at="<%= AgentShellHelper::MEDIUM_AT %>" data-shell-compact-at="<%= AgentShellHelper::COMPACT_AT %>">
  <div class="agent-shell-head" data-test="agent-shell-head"><%= head %></div>
  <div class="agent-shell-status" style="view-transition-name: agent-status;" data-test="agent-shell-status"><%= status %></div>
  <div class="agent-shell-chat" data-test="agent-shell-chat"><%= chat %></div>
</section>
